sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: Nick 2026-11-01, liveness 2026-11-02. Only the Node agent collects facts; doctor reads Gateway state. No Swamp run, no SSH (R1).
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: doctor
  %% kind: doctor.inspect
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane A icon=server pill=observer tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant A as Node agent<br/>orbit-agent
  loop on a short interval
    A->>GW: Heartbeat
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Gateway marks the Node online
    %%> - when heartbeats stop, it marks the Node offline, shown in the web dashboard and in node:list and node:show
  end
  loop continuously, on change
    Note over A: Observe Node state<br/>services, disk, ufw, bridge health
    A->>GW: Report observations<br/>with observed_at
    %%> How:
    %%> - at start, and again when a fact changed
    %%> - a report the Gateway does not accept is sent again after 1, 2 and 4 seconds, and then every 4 seconds until it is accepted
    %%> - the same holds for the request that asks what to watch
    %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06, research thread b8654275):
    %%> - a Node that boots before the Gateway answers reported only at its next read, up to a minute later; with a prompt report Doctor was healthy 15.8 s after boot
    Note over GW: Store latest facts<br/>per Node, per check
  end
  CLI->>GW: doctor
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit doctor`
  %%> - syntax: `doctor [--node=ID] [--family=FAMILY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - without filters, checks all accessible registered Nodes and all families
  Note over GW: Compare facts with intent<br/>exact, drift, missing
  %%> Doctor always answers from the Gateway's state:
  %%> - it never starts a run and never SSHes into the Node
  alt agent online
    GW-->>CLI: Report<br/>agent online · findings
    %%> Result:
    %%> - first line: agent online
    %%> - then the findings; exit 0 with no drift, 1 with drift
  else agent offline
    GW-->>CLI: Report<br/>agent offline since 12:04
    %%> Result:
    %%> - first line: agent offline since <time>
    %%> - the findings still show, each marked "possibly outdated, agent silent since <time>"
    %%> - a nudge to look at the Node agent first
  end
